<Project>

  <!--
    Deliberately empty.

    MSBuild finds the nearest Directory.Build.props by walking up and imports
    only that one, so a file here stops the fixtures in this subtree from
    inheriting tests/Platform.ConsumerConformance/Directory.Build.props, which
    sets Nullable, TreatWarningsAsErrors and a NoWarn list of its own.

    That inheritance has to be broken for these fixtures specifically. They
    assert which properties the policy package asserts, and a property already
    set by a nearer file is skipped by the package's == '' guard - so a
    leftover inherited value would make a package assertion look like a no-op
    and a package non-assertion look like it worked.

    Setting ImportDirectoryBuildProps=false in a fixture's own project body
    does not achieve this: the property is read while
    tests/Platform.ConsumerConformance/Directory.Build.props is being
    imported, long before the body is evaluated.
  -->

</Project>
